ince 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a more humid Mar–May, and this year's shift is substantial. Rainfall shows no clear trend or El Niño link. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 80% chance), about 1 °C above the 1991–2020 average, mostly because of the long-term warming trend rather than El Niño; a wetter-than-normal season is likely (about 75% chance), resting on an El Niño effect that is not clearly established. The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":18.3299,"trend_per_decade":0.2803,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":2.1024,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1533,"enso_p":0.1375,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0304,"intrinsic_sd":0.8116,"effect_this_season":0.3878,"effect_ratio":0.4778,"size":"Noticeable","size_typical_el_nino":"Noticeable","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":1.0007,"forecast_mean":19.3306,"forecast_sd":0.8799,"p_below":0.0943,"p_near":0.1023,"p_above":0.8034,"forecast_words":"Likely (80%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"trend_part_2027":0.6129,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":13.8329,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.3638,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.0045,"enso_p":0.9753,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":-0.0113,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.2992,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1906,"enso_p":0.1041,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.4822,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.1